:END:
#+title: Presets
#+auto_tangle: t
#+PROPERTY: header-args:zig :tangle ../../../src/cft-code/presets.zig :mkdirp yes

#+interface:

Presets are the physics-facing constructors for common CFT data.  They sit
between [[id:20260605T090102.250727][Theory]] and [[id:20260606T150002.000000][CFT Kernel]]: a user asks for a free
boson, a \(bc\) system, a product, or a boundary extension, and receives a small
generated type with operator builders and correlator entry points.

This file is intentionally modest.  The current kernel does not yet execute
Wick contractions, so these presets establish the API and stable operator
families without pretending to compute correlators.  The lowering to compact
rule tables will happen inside the future DSL.

#+begin_src zig
const operators = @import("expressions/operators.zig");
const coefficient = @import("expressions/coefficient.zig");
const theory = @import("theory/theory.zig");
const tensor = @import("tensor-code");
#+end_src

* Handles And Conventions

The preset API uses handles, not owned symbolic payloads.  This keeps the user
surface compact and lets later stores decide how momenta, profiles, tensors,
and Chan-Paton factors are represented.

#+begin_src zig
/// Handle groups compact ids used by preset operator builders.
pub const Handle = struct {
    /// Coord names a holomorphic or antiholomorphic coordinate variable.
    pub const Coord = coefficient.Variable;
    /// BoundaryCoord names a real boundary coordinate variable.
    pub const BoundaryCoord = coefficient.Variable;
    /// Index names a target-space vector index.
    pub const Index = u32;
    /// Momentum names a target-space momentum expression.
    pub const Momentum = u32;
    /// Profile names a selected presentation of a target-space profile.
    pub const Profile = u32;
    /// TargetFunction names a position-space target profile.
    pub const TargetFunction = u32;
    /// FourierTransform names a Fourier-space target profile.
    pub const FourierTransform = u32;
    /// TargetPoint names a point in target space.
    pub const TargetPoint = u32;
    /// TensorProjector names a tensor-code projector expression.
    pub const TensorProjector = tensor.kernel.TensorExprId;
    /// BoundaryStack names stacked boundary-condition Chan-Paton data.
    pub const BoundaryStack = u32;
    /// PolynomialProfileTerm stores one finite polynomial profile term.
    pub const PolynomialProfileTerm = struct {
        coefficient: u32,
        power: u16,
    };
};

/// ConventionScalar stores small convention constants used by preset builders.
pub const ConventionScalar = union(enum) {
    one,
    rational: struct { numerator: i64, denominator: i64 },
    symbol: []const u8,
};

/// FreeBosonConvention selects the normalization convention for the free boson.
pub const FreeBosonConvention = enum {
    stringbook,
    prototype,
};
#+end_src

The default free-boson convention follows the stringbook normalization
\[
  T^X=-{1\over \alpha'}\,\partial X^\mu\partial X_\mu,
\]
and the corresponding Polyakov/free-field conventions [cite:@yinStringbook].
The \(bc\) preset uses
\[
  b(z)c(0)\sim {1\over z},\qquad
  T^{\rm gh}=-(\partial b)c-2b\partial c,
\]
and the sphere normalization
\[
  \left\langle\prod_{i=1}^3 c(z_i)\tilde c(\bar z_i)\right\rangle
  = |z_{12}z_{13}z_{23}|^2
\]
[cite:@yinStringbook].

* Operator Helpers

For now an operator body id is just a stable kind number.  The future body store
will attach label spans for indices, momenta, profiles, derivative labels, and
Chan-Paton factors.  We do not allocate such a store here.

#+begin_src zig
const BodyKind = enum(operators.OperatorBodyId) {
    x = 1,
    d_x = 2,
    d_xt = 3,
    exp_x = 4,
    profile_x = 5,
    b = 16,
    c = 17,
    bt = 18,
    ct = 19,
    d_x_boundary = 32,
    exp_x_boundary = 33,
    profile_x_boundary = 34,
    b_boundary = 48,
    c_boundary = 49,
};

fn pairInsertion(z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.OperatorInsertion {
    return .{ .pair = .{
        .holomorphic_position = z,
        .antiholomorphic_position = zbar,
        .holomorphic_derivatives = 0,
        .antiholomorphic_derivatives = 0,
    } };
}

fn singleInsertion(z: Handle.Coord, derivatives: u8) operators.OperatorInsertion {
    return .{ .single = .{
        .position = z,
        .derivatives = derivatives,
    } };
}

fn operator(kind: BodyKind, insertion: operators.OperatorInsertion) operators.Operator {
    return .{
        .insertion = insertion,
        .body = @intFromEnum(kind),
    };
}
#+end_src

* Free Boson

The free boson preset is a bulk theory.  Its public data is just dimension and
normalization choice.  \(SO(D)\) tensor invariants and momentum algebra are
handled by [[id:20260605T075909.433647][Tensor-Code]] later; the preset only fixes the operator families.

#+begin_src zig
/// FreeBosonConfig declares a noncompact D-dimensional free boson preset.
pub const FreeBosonConfig = struct {
    dimension: u16,
    alpha_prime: ConventionScalar = .{ .symbol = "alpha_prime" },
    convention: FreeBosonConvention = .stringbook,
    explicit_x: bool = true,
};

/// freeBoson builds the API type for a noncompact free-boson CFT.
pub fn freeBoson(comptime cfg: FreeBosonConfig) type {
    return struct {
        const preset_kind = PresetKind.free_boson;
        const preset_config = cfg;

        /// op exposes free-boson local operator builders.
        pub const op = FreeBosonOp;
        /// profile exposes profile-presentation builders.
        pub const profile = ProfileOp;
        /// config exposes named correlator configs for this preset.
        pub const config = SphereConfig;

        /// correlator evaluates free-boson insertions with a compiled config.
        pub fn correlator(config_ptr: *const theory.Runtime.CorrelatorConfig, ops: anytype, sink: anytype) !void {
            _ = config_ptr;
            _ = ops;
            _ = sink;
            return error.NotImplemented;
        }
    };
}
#+end_src

The derivative label convention is \(dX(\mu,n,z)=\partial^{n+1}X^\mu(z)\).
An explicit \(X\) body is present because position-space profiles and NLSM
expansions naturally produce logarithmic Green kernels.

#+begin_src zig
const FreeBosonOp = struct {
    /// X builds an explicit bulk free-boson field insertion.
    pub fn X(mu: Handle.Index, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        _ = mu;
        return operator(.x, pairInsertion(z, zbar));
    }

    /// dX builds a holomorphic derivative field insertion.
    pub fn dX(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        _ = mu;
        return operator(.d_x, singleInsertion(z, n));
    }

    /// dXt builds an antiholomorphic derivative field insertion.
    pub fn dXt(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        _ = mu;
        return operator(.d_xt, singleInsertion(zbar, n));
    }

    /// expX builds a normal-ordered plane-wave insertion.
    pub fn expX(k: Handle.Momentum, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        _ = k;
        return operator(.exp_x, pairInsertion(z, zbar));
    }

    /// profile builds a target-space profile insertion.
    pub fn profile(f: Handle.Profile, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        _ = f;
        return operator(.profile_x, pairInsertion(z, zbar));
    }
};
#+end_src

Profiles are presentation handles.  Position-space profiles keep the zero-mode
integral explicit; Fourier profiles reduce to plane waves; polynomial profiles
support Riemann-normal-coordinate expansions.

#+begin_src zig
const ProfileOp = struct {
    /// positionSpace selects the exact residual position-space profile presentation.
    pub fn positionSpace(f: Handle.TargetFunction) Handle.Profile {
        return f;
    }

    /// fourier selects the Fourier-space profile presentation.
    pub fn fourier(f_hat: Handle.FourierTransform) Handle.Profile {
        return f_hat;
    }

    /// polynomialRnc selects a finite polynomial profile presentation.
    pub fn polynomialRnc(point: Handle.TargetPoint, terms: []const Handle.PolynomialProfileTerm) Handle.Profile {
        _ = terms;
        return point;
    }
};
#+end_src

* bc Sphere

The \(bc\) sphere preset is independent of the matter CFT.  Stringbook fixes
the local OPE \(b(z)c(0)\sim z^{-1}\), the weights \(h_b=2\),
\(h_c=-1\), and the sphere top-form normalization [cite:@yinStringbook].

#+begin_src zig
/// BcSphereConfig declares the holomorphic bc system and optional antiholomorphic copy.
pub const BcSphereConfig = struct {
    include_antiholomorphic_copy: bool = true,
};

/// bcSphere builds the API type for the sphere bc ghost CFT.
pub fn bcSphere(comptime cfg: BcSphereConfig) type {
    return struct {
        const preset_kind = PresetKind.bc_sphere;
        const preset_config = cfg;

        /// op exposes bc ghost local operator builders.
        pub const op = BcSphereOp;
        /// config exposes named correlator configs for this preset.
        pub const config = SphereConfig;

        /// correlator evaluates bc insertions with a compiled config.
        pub fn correlator(config_ptr: *const theory.Runtime.CorrelatorConfig, ops: anytype, sink: anytype) !void {
            _ = config_ptr;
            _ = ops;
            _ = sink;
            return error.NotImplemented;
        }
    };
}
#+end_src

Derivative labels mean \(\partial^n b\), \(\partial^n c\), and the
antiholomorphic copies.

#+begin_src zig
const BcSphereOp = struct {
    /// b builds a holomorphic b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn b(n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return operator(.b, singleInsertion(z, n));
    }

    /// c builds a holomorphic c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn c(n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return operator(.c, singleInsertion(z, n));
    }

    /// bt builds an antiholomorphic b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn bt(n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return operator(.bt, singleInsertion(zbar, n));
    }

    /// ct builds an antiholomorphic c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn ct(n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return operator(.ct, singleInsertion(zbar, n));
    }
};
#+end_src

* Product

Tensor products are products of sector data and quantum-number lists.  There is
no runtime tensor-product payload.  At this milestone the product API exposes
the implemented bulk builders directly: free bosons and \(bc\) ghosts.

#+begin_src zig
/// product builds the API type for a product of independent bulk presets.
pub fn product(comptime factors: anytype) type {
    return struct {
        const preset_kind = PresetKind.product;
        const preset_factors = factors;

        /// op exposes the joined operator builders of the product factors.
        pub const op = ProductOp(factors);
        /// config exposes named correlator configs for this product preset.
        pub const config = SphereConfig;

        /// correlator evaluates product-theory insertions with a compiled config.
        pub fn correlator(config_ptr: *const theory.Runtime.CorrelatorConfig, ops: anytype, sink: anytype) !void {
            _ = config_ptr;
            _ = ops;
            _ = sink;
            return error.NotImplemented;
        }
    };
}

fn ProductOp(comptime factors: anytype) type {
    _ = factors;
    return BulkProductOp;
}

const BulkProductOp = struct {
    /// X builds an explicit bulk free-boson field insertion.
    pub fn X(mu: Handle.Index, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonOp.X(mu, z, zbar);
    }

    /// dX builds a holomorphic derivative field insertion.
    pub fn dX(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonOp.dX(mu, n, z);
    }

    /// dXt builds an antiholomorphic derivative field insertion.
    pub fn dXt(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonOp.dXt(mu, n, zbar);
    }

    /// expX builds a normal-ordered plane-wave insertion.
    pub fn expX(k: Handle.Momentum, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonOp.expX(k, z, zbar);
    }

    /// profile builds a target-space profile insertion.
    pub fn profile(f: Handle.Profile, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonOp.profile(f, z, zbar);
    }

    /// b builds a holomorphic b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn b(n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BcSphereOp.b(n, z);
    }

    /// c builds a holomorphic c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn c(n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BcSphereOp.c(n, z);
    }

    /// bt builds an antiholomorphic b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn bt(n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BcSphereOp.bt(n, zbar);
    }

    /// ct builds an antiholomorphic c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn ct(n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BcSphereOp.ct(n, zbar);
    }
};
#+end_src

* Boundary Extensions

The bulk CFT remains boundary-free.  A BCFT is formed only by applying boundary
extensions to a chosen bulk theory.  This mirrors the stringbook distinction
between the bulk field and its boundary limit.  In particular,
\[
  \partial^n X(y)=\lim_{z\to y}\partial^nX(z),
\]
and \(\partial X(y)\) is not \(\partial_yX(y)\): for Neumann
\(\partial_yX=2\partial X\), while for Dirichlet \(\partial_yX=0\)
[cite:@yinStringbook].

#+begin_src zig
const BoundaryExtensionKind = enum {
    free_boson_boundary,
    bc_disk,
};

const BoundaryExtension = struct {
    kind: BoundaryExtensionKind,
    chan_paton: ?Handle.BoundaryStack = null,
};

/// FreeBosonBoundaryConfig declares Neumann and Dirichlet data for a brane.
pub const FreeBosonBoundaryConfig = struct {
    neumann: Handle.TensorProjector,
    dirichlet: Handle.TensorProjector,
    dirichlet_position: Handle.TargetPoint,
    chan_paton: ?Handle.BoundaryStack = null,
};

/// freeBosonBoundary declares the Neumann/Dirichlet free-boson boundary extension.
pub fn freeBosonBoundary(comptime cfg: FreeBosonBoundaryConfig) BoundaryExtension {
    _ = cfg.neumann;
    _ = cfg.dirichlet;
    _ = cfg.dirichlet_position;
    return .{ .kind = .free_boson_boundary, .chan_paton = cfg.chan_paton };
}
#+end_src

The boundary free-boson builders expose stringbook's holomorphic boundary
limit.  A real boundary derivative can be built later at expression level if a
client wants it.

#+begin_src zig
const FreeBosonBoundaryOp = struct {
    /// dXBoundary builds stringbook's holomorphic boundary limit of dX.
    pub fn dXBoundary(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        _ = mu;
        return operator(.d_x_boundary, singleInsertion(y, n));
    }

    /// expXBoundary builds a Neumann boundary plane-wave insertion.
    pub fn expXBoundary(k: Handle.Momentum, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        _ = k;
        return operator(.exp_x_boundary, singleInsertion(y, 0));
    }

    /// profileBoundary builds a boundary profile insertion.
    pub fn profileBoundary(f: Handle.Profile, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        _ = f;
        return operator(.profile_x_boundary, singleInsertion(y, 0));
    }
};
#+end_src

The boundary \(bc\) extension supplies boundary ghosts and mixed bulk-boundary
rules for disk amplitudes.  The rules are not executed here yet; they are part
of the future lowered Wick table.

#+begin_src zig
/// BcDiskConfig declares the disk boundary extension for the bc ghost system.
pub const BcDiskConfig = struct {
    include_mixed_bulk_boundary: bool = true,
};

/// bcDiskBoundary declares boundary and mixed bulk-boundary bc rules on the disk.
pub fn bcDiskBoundary(comptime cfg: BcDiskConfig) BoundaryExtension {
    _ = cfg;
    return .{ .kind = .bc_disk };
}

const BcDiskBoundaryOp = struct {
    /// bBoundary builds a boundary b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn bBoundary(n: u8, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return operator(.b_boundary, singleInsertion(y, n));
    }

    /// cBoundary builds a boundary c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn cBoundary(n: u8, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return operator(.c_boundary, singleInsertion(y, n));
    }
};
#+end_src

The boundary builder merges the bulk operator namespace with the selected
boundary namespaces.  Chan-Paton data remains an optional label on boundary
extensions and may point to tensor-code structures later.

#+begin_src zig
/// boundary builds the API type for a BCFT from a bulk preset and boundary extensions.
pub fn boundary(comptime Bulk: type, comptime extensions: anytype) type {
    return struct {
        const preset_kind = PresetKind.boundary;
        const bulk = Bulk;
        const boundary_extensions = extensions;

        /// op exposes bulk and boundary operator builders.
        pub const op = BoundaryOp(Bulk, extensions);
        /// config exposes named correlator configs for this BCFT.
        pub const config = DiskConfig;

        /// correlator evaluates BCFT insertions with a compiled config.
        pub fn correlator(config_ptr: *const theory.Runtime.CorrelatorConfig, ops: anytype, sink: anytype) !void {
            _ = config_ptr;
            _ = ops;
            _ = sink;
            return error.NotImplemented;
        }
    };
}

fn BoundaryOp(comptime Bulk: type, comptime extensions: anytype) type {
    _ = Bulk;
    _ = extensions;
    return BoundaryProductOp;
}

const BoundaryProductOp = struct {
    /// X builds an explicit bulk free-boson field insertion.
    pub fn X(mu: Handle.Index, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.X(mu, z, zbar);
    }

    /// dX builds a holomorphic derivative field insertion.
    pub fn dX(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.dX(mu, n, z);
    }

    /// dXt builds an antiholomorphic derivative field insertion.
    pub fn dXt(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.dXt(mu, n, zbar);
    }

    /// expX builds a normal-ordered plane-wave insertion.
    pub fn expX(k: Handle.Momentum, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.expX(k, z, zbar);
    }

    /// profile builds a target-space profile insertion.
    pub fn profile(f: Handle.Profile, z: Handle.Coord, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.profile(f, z, zbar);
    }

    /// b builds a holomorphic b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn b(n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.b(n, z);
    }

    /// c builds a holomorphic c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn c(n: u8, z: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.c(n, z);
    }

    /// bt builds an antiholomorphic b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn bt(n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.bt(n, zbar);
    }

    /// ct builds an antiholomorphic c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn ct(n: u8, zbar: Handle.Coord) operators.Operator {
        return BulkProductOp.ct(n, zbar);
    }

    /// dXBoundary builds stringbook's holomorphic boundary limit of dX.
    pub fn dXBoundary(mu: Handle.Index, n: u8, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonBoundaryOp.dXBoundary(mu, n, y);
    }

    /// expXBoundary builds a Neumann boundary plane-wave insertion.
    pub fn expXBoundary(k: Handle.Momentum, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonBoundaryOp.expXBoundary(k, y);
    }

    /// profileBoundary builds a boundary profile insertion.
    pub fn profileBoundary(f: Handle.Profile, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return FreeBosonBoundaryOp.profileBoundary(f, y);
    }

    /// bBoundary builds a boundary b-ghost insertion.
    pub fn bBoundary(n: u8, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return BcDiskBoundaryOp.bBoundary(n, y);
    }

    /// cBoundary builds a boundary c-ghost insertion.
    pub fn cBoundary(n: u8, y: Handle.BoundaryCoord) operators.Operator {
        return BcDiskBoundaryOp.cBoundary(n, y);
    }
};
#+end_src

* Minimal Config Data

The correlator receives a pointer to a compact config.  The numeric ids here
are placeholders until the DSL lowers presets into [[id:20260605T090102.250727][Theory]] rule tables.

#+begin_src zig
const SphereConfig = struct {
    /// sphere selects sphere Wick and zero-mode rules.
    pub const sphere = theory.Runtime.CorrelatorConfig{
        .wick_rules = 0,
        .zero_modes = 0,
    };
};

const DiskConfig = struct {
    /// disk selects disk Wick and zero-mode rules.
    pub const disk = theory.Runtime.CorrelatorConfig{
        .wick_rules = 1,
        .zero_modes = 1,
    };
};
#+end_src

* Private Data

The only private generic data left here is the preset tag used by generated
types.  The actual rule tables remain future DSL output.

#+begin_src zig
const PresetKind = enum {
    free_boson,
    bc_sphere,
    product,
    boundary,
};
#+end_src

* API Check

This test checks one concept: the public preset API composes bulk factors and
boundary extensions without asking the caller to touch theory internals.

#+begin_src zig
test "presets compose operator builders without exposing theory tables" {
    const testing = @import("std").testing;

    const FreeBoson = freeBoson(.{ .dimension = 26 });
    const BosonicSphere = product(.{ FreeBoson, bcSphere(.{}) });
    const BosonicDisk = boundary(BosonicSphere, .{
        freeBosonBoundary(.{
            .neumann = 1,
            .dirichlet = 2,
            .dirichlet_position = 3,
        }),
        bcDiskBoundary(.{}),
    });

    const x = BosonicDisk.op.expXBoundary(4, 10);
    const c = BosonicDisk.op.cBoundary(0, 11);

    try testing.expectEqual(@intFromEnum(BodyKind.exp_x_boundary), x.body);
    try testing.expectEqual(@intFromEnum(BodyKind.c_boundary), c.body);
}
#+end_src
